/* sapling.sas: load the Sapling macro library. A program sets SPL_ROOT (the folder that holds
   macros/) first:
     %LET spl_root = /path/of/the/study;
     %INCLUDE "&spl_root./macros/sapling.sas";
   Each macro is one file with its header (docs/sas-style.md). The macros you call come first;
   those that start with _spl_ are their inner parts (checks, the text of a number, the result
   shape, the rows of a table, the look of a figure). The printer %print writes each table and
   listing as RTF and as a monospace listing; a figure macro (%kmplot, %meanplot ...) its figure
   as PNG and RTF.
   License: Commercial, DataStep Labs (see LICENSE). */
